    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "JAPAN AIR LINES\nEt An 2",
      "Chrysanthemum and Stream by Ogata Koorin (1658~1716)\neam Dy\nla Koorin (165\nOne of Japan's endurig art forms.\nthe decorated fan in a beautiful and\nuseful device widely popular even today. It has a wide range of uses,\nserving as an integral part of many classical dances, and a diverse\nnumber of other uses, including, of course; that of cooling the brow\nThe design for this fan is a stylized stream and chrysanthemums,\nJapan's national flower. Executed on a gold ground, the red and yellow\n00 0\nchrysanthemums have been applied with an impasto technique in combi-\nnation with leaves painted in an abbreviated style. Those elements.\ntogether with the stylized stream, produce a splendid effect. The art-\nist, Koorin, was one of Japan's greatest decorative painters.\nJAL hopes this hand-made fan will serve as a remembrance of our\nservice to you.\nJAPAN AIR LINES\n(1658~1716)"
    ],
